WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.400
Well, hi everyone. I wanted to take a few minutes to share with you our vision for the

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:12.320
new church that we're launching on Sunday, November 3rd, in the Sachse-Garland area.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.719
And this video, it's going to be a little bit lengthy. It will have three parts. Part

00:00:16.719 --> 00:00:21.719
one, I will share our vision. Part two, I'll share our values. And then in part three,

00:00:21.719 --> 00:00:28.400
I'll share details on the where and when and how you can get involved, if you're so inclined.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:35.040
So let's start with part one, the vision. So it seems to me that the great temptation,

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:40.360
and perhaps this is true of any age, but specifically of our age, is that we're very tempted to

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:46.680
be incredibly reactionary, right? And I think this is true at both the micro and the macro

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:51.279
level. Let's start with the micro or like the individual level. At the micro level,

00:00:51.279 --> 00:00:56.160
because we're human, we are tempted to operate from an incredibly reactionary place, right?

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:00.639
We're tempted to operate from the worst version of ourselves, right? We're shot through with

00:01:00.639 --> 00:01:07.760
anxiety, and what if, and so we react. We are stressed out, and so we react. We're afraid,

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:12.800
and so we react. In fact, if you look at your own life and the lives of others, you probably

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:17.639
see this reactionary posture all over the place. By the way, this is what the Bible

00:01:17.639 --> 00:01:24.639
calls sin, because it's bad. It hurts people, right? We hurt people. I hurt people. However,

00:01:25.239 --> 00:01:30.639
when it gets crazy is when this starts to play out at the macro level. You see, in our

00:01:30.639 --> 00:01:35.599
culture, in our politics, in our religious institutions, we have some very loud voices

00:01:35.599 --> 00:01:42.599
that are basically 24-7 fear, outrage, and anger machines. And what this is leading to

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:49.480
is an incredible level of polarization, right? It's us against them. My people versus your

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:53.959
people. My religion versus your religion. My political group versus your political group.

00:01:53.959 --> 00:01:58.279
And unfortunately, many churches and church leaders, rather than opposing this, seem

00:01:58.279 --> 00:02:05.279
to be joining right in, right? They say, there is a culture war, and sadly, a lot of Christians

00:02:07.199 --> 00:02:13.240
and folks are like the people banging the war drums the loudest. And I believe that's

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:20.199
a tragedy, but it's a sign that we live in a reactionary age. Okay, so what's the good

00:02:20.199 --> 00:02:25.160
news here? Well, I believe that this church community we're launching has a tremendous

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:32.160
opportunity to be an oasis of calm in the midst of the storm, a light in the darkness.

00:02:33.679 --> 00:02:39.119
Because while the culture wants us to go to war with one another, we are going to choose

00:02:39.119 --> 00:02:45.880
instead to gather at the table. That's the name of our church, the table. I want you

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:51.399
to think of a table. What is a table a picture of? Well, it's a lot of things, right? It's

00:02:51.399 --> 00:02:58.399
a picture of family. It's a picture of community, right? It's a picture of love and of sharing,

00:03:02.279 --> 00:03:08.600
of food, and it's a picture of a place where enemies can listen to one another, understand

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:13.960
one another, right? It's a picture of a place where I can know and be known, where I can

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:20.960
seek to understand and be understood. It's a place where I can learn, as the message

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:26.960
version, the paraphrase of the Bible says, I can learn the unforced rhythms of grace.

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:32.000
And if you place the table in the context of a church, well then that table becomes

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:38.199
much more than simply a regular old table. It becomes the table of the Lord Jesus, the

00:03:38.199 --> 00:03:44.919
Jesus who said, love your enemies and pray for those who persecute you. The Jesus who

00:03:44.919 --> 00:03:49.960
was the friend of sinners, the Jesus who, as the writer Jean Leclerc said, he ate good

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:56.759
food with bad people. I love that. The Jesus who said, why are you anxious? Don't you know

00:03:56.759 --> 00:04:03.759
that God loves you and sees you? The Jesus who died and rose again to draw all people

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:11.000
to himself. The Jesus who, on the night he was betrayed, stood at what? A table and said,

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:20.440
this bread is my body, broken for you. This wine is my blood, shed for you. Remember me.

00:04:20.679 --> 00:04:25.959
Remember me, never forget. So this is who we are, as an organization and as a church.

00:04:25.959 --> 00:04:32.959
The table exists to shift a generation from reactionary to visionary, to the person in

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:39.720
work of Jesus. You see, what the world needs is visionary people. People who can say, I

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:44.880
don't have to be insecure. I don't have to be afraid. I don't have to be alone, because

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:51.880
the God I've come to know in Jesus is love. And I'm his child. And I have a church community

00:04:52.559 --> 00:04:59.559
that expresses that and reminds me of that in everything we say and do. Okay, so that's

00:05:00.559 --> 00:05:07.559
part one. Part two is our core values. So this starts to name, what on earth are the

00:05:08.519 --> 00:05:14.720
values that will actually keep us aligned with this vision? So here at the table we

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:21.720
have five values. Number one, thoughtful. Number two, inclusive. Three, eclectic. Four,

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:29.160
communal. Number five, vulnerable. Okay, so let's unpack these. Number one, I said, is

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:36.200
thoughtful. We are a community that values a thoughtful approach to life. We're okay

00:05:37.959 --> 00:05:43.640
with things taking a little bit of time. We want to go a little bit slowly. We want to

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:48.200
think it through. We want to weigh the cost of our words and the implications of our actions.

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:55.440
You see, to be thoughtful means that there are no questions or issues that we are unwilling

00:05:56.079 --> 00:06:03.079
to tackle. Instead, we seek to mirror both the calm and the depth of Christ, for whom

00:06:04.079 --> 00:06:11.079
nothing was off limits. Number two is the value for being inclusive. So we are a radically

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:18.279
inclusive community. You see, the reactionary mind is constantly searching for an enemy

00:06:18.279 --> 00:06:25.279
to exclude, but we keep searching for new people to bring to the table. We keep stretching,

00:06:26.079 --> 00:06:31.480
stretching, stretching the definitions of who might be valued and welcomed into God's

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:38.480
kingdom. So no matter what socioeconomic bracket, your racial identity, sexual orientation,

00:06:38.679 --> 00:06:45.679
mental facility, or moral standing, we want to create a table big enough to hold everyone.

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:53.160
Number three is eclectic. Now, radical inclusivity means that we want to live into that, the

00:06:53.160 --> 00:07:00.160
tension of that, that difference creates, and we want to celebrate the beautiful chaos

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:05.559
of it all. This means we are a remarkably eclectic community. We think there's beauty

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:11.920
in bringing unexpected people, unexpected ideas, and traditions of Christianity together

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:18.920
because it's in that place of creative tension that new life happens. That's why we want

00:07:19.359 --> 00:07:25.320
and we need people of differing theologies, politics, personalities, and giftedness in

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:32.320
one community. Sure, it's super uncomfortable at times, but we're all better off for it

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:38.920
because without the new and the different, we cannot stretch and grow.

00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:45.920
Number four, communal. We are a church devoted to the principles of communion. See, to participate

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:54.640
in communion is to lean into the mystery of Christ's present nearness. As a communal church,

00:07:55.640 --> 00:08:02.640
we are committed to being present to one another, to allow the depth that is fostered in being

00:08:04.279 --> 00:08:11.119
in communion with one another to resonate out into the world around us. We believe that

00:08:11.119 --> 00:08:17.920
to be in communion with one another is to participate in the restorative, renewing life

00:08:17.959 --> 00:08:19.679
of Christ.

00:08:19.679 --> 00:08:25.200
Core value number five is vulnerable. This is a hard one, but it's absolutely essential.

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:30.160
See, we are a church that is committed to vulnerability as it is. It's basically the

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:36.599
linchpin to all of our other values. It takes vulnerability to be introspective in the way

00:08:36.599 --> 00:08:42.500
that thoughtfulness requires. It takes vulnerability to allow the risks and challenges in the way

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:49.500
inclusivity requires. It takes vulnerability to do the work of synthesizing eclectic ideas

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:55.859
and making room for the ways that our assumptions will be challenged when we do that. And it

00:08:55.859 --> 00:09:01.539
takes vulnerability to foster the kind of depth and relational intimacy that communion

00:09:01.539 --> 00:09:02.580
inspires.

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:09.580
Okay, so that is part two of our core values. The third and final part is the details, the

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:16.580
where, the when, the how. Okay, so where are we meeting? Well, the plan right now is that

00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:23.580
we will be renting a space at a church in Sachse, Texas at 5 p.m. on Sunday evenings.

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:28.179
I can't yet say which church because we haven't inked that contract, but we're very close

00:09:28.179 --> 00:09:34.059
to finalizing it. So, Sachse, Texas. When will we begin meeting? Our first public service

00:09:35.059 --> 00:09:39.059
will be Sunday, November 3rd. I'm pumped.

00:09:39.059 --> 00:09:44.659
All right, how? How can you be a part? Well, there's three ways. First, join the launch

00:09:44.659 --> 00:09:51.659
team. The launch team are people who say more than, I will attend. They say, I will pray,

00:09:51.859 --> 00:09:57.219
serve, give. In essence, these are the people who say, look, I believe in what you're doing

00:09:57.219 --> 00:10:01.780
and I want to be in at the ground level, helping to make it a reality.

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:06.460
There may be those who say, though, well, that sounds like a lot. I'm not sure I can

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:09.820
be a part of the launch team, but I still want to help. All right, second option, you

00:10:09.820 --> 00:10:14.099
can attend. Like I said, we'll be launching November 3rd, and so if you want to stay in

00:10:14.099 --> 00:10:20.179
the loop on that, simply kick me an email at brettatthetabletx.com or direct message

00:10:20.179 --> 00:10:25.739
me via like really any social media outlet. Third, of course, you can give. I'll link

00:10:25.739 --> 00:10:30.700
to our giving page below, but if this is a vision that you really believe in, then we

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:35.900
would greatly appreciate your support. Okay, I hope you enjoyed this video. Please like

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:40.299
it, share it, and remember, stay humble, stay kind. God bless.

